+# Deploying Fizzy on one server
+
+The default `config/deploy.yml` runs Fizzy, SQLite, local file storage, and Solid
+Queue background jobs in **one application container**. Kamal runs a separate
+proxy that obtains and renews Let's Encrypt certificates. No MySQL, Redis, S3,
+or separate job server is needed. This setup does not use the private SaaS gem.
+
+## Prerequisites
+
+- A Linux server with Docker, reachable over SSH (root by default, or a user with
+  Docker permissions configured under `ssh` in the deployment config).
+- A hostname whose DNS A record (and AAAA record, if present) points to the server.
+  Ports 80 and 443 must be publicly reachable and free for Kamal Proxy. Do not put
+  another TLS-terminating proxy in front of it for this setup.
+- An SMTP service and a verified sender address. Email is required for sign-in.
+- On your development machine: the Ruby version in `.ruby-version`, Bundler,
+  Docker with Buildx, and SSH access to the server. Run `bundle install` in your
+  fork. You don't need to run `bin/setup` or configure a local database to deploy.
+
+## Configure your fork
+
+1. Edit `config/deploy.yml`:
+   - Replace `fizzy.example.com` under `servers.web` with your hostname (no scheme
+     or path). The YAML alias also sets the proxy host and `APP_FQDN` for links.
+     If SSH uses a different address, put that address under `servers.web` and
+     set `proxy.host` and `APP_FQDN` explicitly to the public hostname.
+   - Set `MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS`, `SMTP_ADDRESS`, `SMTP_PORT`, and
+     `SMTP_AUTHENTICATION` to match your mail service. Defaults use authenticated
+     SMTP with STARTTLS on port 587. For implicit TLS on port 465, also add
+     `SMTP_SSL: "true"` and `SMTP_ENABLE_STARTTLS_AUTO: "false"` to `env.clear`.
+     `SMTP_DOMAIN` optionally overrides the EHLO domain (defaults to `APP_FQDN`).
+     For an unauthenticated relay, set `SMTP_AUTHENTICATION: ""` and remove the
+     SMTP username/password entries from `env.secret`.
+   - Set `builder.arch` to your server's architecture (`amd64` or `arm64`).
+     `WEB_CONCURRENCY` and `JOB_CONCURRENCY` start at one for smaller machines.
+
+2. Create your local secrets file:
+
+   ```sh
+   cp .kamal/secrets.example .kamal/secrets
+   chmod 600 .kamal/secrets
+   bin/rails secret
+   ```
+
+   Paste the generated value into `SECRET_KEY_BASE` in `.kamal/secrets`, and fill
+   in your SMTP credentials. This is a dotenv file, not YAML; quote values with
+   spaces or special characters as needed. Keep this file private and backed up.
+   It is ignored by Git and excluded from Docker builds. No `RAILS_MASTER_KEY`
+   is required for this setup; it uses environment secrets rather than encrypted
+   Rails credentials. Keep `SECRET_KEY_BASE` stable across deploys.
+
+   Browser push notifications are optional. To enable them, generate a key pair:
+
+   ```sh
+   bundle exec ruby -rweb-push -e 'key = WebPush.generate_key; puts "VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=#{key.public_key}", "VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=#{key.private_key}"'
+   ```
+
+   Uncomment the VAPID entries in both the secrets file and `env.secret`, and
+   paste in the keys. Keep this pair stable too.
+
+3. Commit your configuration changes. Kamal builds from the Git checkout, so
+   uncommitted changes are not included in the image. Never commit secrets.
+
+## Deploy
+
+```sh
+bundle exec kamal setup
+```
+
+This builds the root Dockerfile, transfers the image via Kamal's local registry
+(`localhost:5555`, forwarded over SSH; no registry account needed), starts the
+proxy, and boots Fizzy. The image entrypoint runs `db:prepare` before serving
+traffic, creating or migrating all SQLite databases. Visit `https://your-host`
+and sign up with an email address you can receive mail at.
+
+For subsequent releases, commit your changes and run:
+
+```sh
+bundle exec kamal deploy
+```
+
+Useful commands:
+
+```sh
+bundle exec kamal logs
+bundle exec kamal console
+bundle exec kamal shell
+```
+
+## Persistent data and backups
+
+The named Docker volume `fizzy_storage` is mounted at `/rails/storage`. It holds
+all four production SQLite databases (application, jobs, cache, and Action Cable)
+and uploaded files under `storage/production/files`. New releases reuse it, so
+normal deploys and container replacements preserve data. Jobs, including recurring
+tasks, run through Solid Queue's Puma plugin on the same box.
+
+Do not change the volume name or delete it when deploying. A persistent volume
+is **not a backup**: take regular off-server backups of the entire volume and keep
+your secrets separately. Stop the app (including its embedded jobs) with
+`bundle exec kamal app stop` before copying the volume for a consistent backup,
+and restart it with `bundle exec kamal app start` afterward. Test your restores.
+Do not copy only a live SQLite database file and omit its WAL files.
+
+This configuration is for a single server, not horizontal scaling or automatic
+failover. Moving to a different server requires restoring the data volume and
+secrets there.
diff --git a/test/deployment-test b/test/deployment-test
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..10de205
--- /dev/null
+++ b/test/deployment-test
@@ -0,0 +1,122 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env ruby
+# Run with: bundle exec ruby test/deployment-test
+require "minitest/autorun"
+require "yaml"
+require "pathname"
+require "open3"
+require "tmpdir"
+require "kamal"
+
+class DeploymentTest < Minitest::Test
+  def setup
+    @root = File.expand_path("..", __dir__)
+    @config = Kamal::Configuration.create_from(config_file: Pathname.new("#{@root}/config/deploy.yml"), version: "test")
+    @raw = @config.raw_config
+  end
+
+  def test_single_box_with_proxy_tls_and_embedded_jobs
+    assert_equal [ "web" ], @raw.servers.keys
+    assert_equal 1, @raw.servers.fetch("web").size
+    assert_equal true, @raw.proxy.fetch("ssl")
+    assert_equal 80, @raw.proxy.fetch("app_port")
+    assert_equal @raw.proxy.fetch("host"), @config.env.clear.fetch("APP_FQDN")
+    assert_equal "true", @config.env.clear.fetch("SOLID_QUEUE_IN_PUMA")
+    assert_equal "sqlite", @config.env.clear.fetch("DATABASE_ADAPTER")
+    assert_equal "local", @config.env.clear.fetch("ACTIVE_STORAGE_SERVICE")
+    assert_empty @config.accessories
+    assert @config.registry.local?
+  end
+
+  def test_data_is_in_a_named_volume
+    assert_includes @raw.volumes, "fizzy_storage:/rails/storage"
+    databases = YAML.load_file("#{@root}/config/database.sqlite.yml", aliases: true).fetch("production")
+    assert_equal %w[ cable cache primary queue ], databases.keys.sort
+    databases.each_value do |database|
+      assert database.fetch("database").start_with?("storage/"), "Database must live in the persistent volume"
+    end
+    assert_equal "/rails/public/assets", @raw.asset_path
+  end
+
+  def test_secrets_are_not_cleartext_configuration
+    assert_includes @config.env.secret_keys, "SECRET_KEY_BASE"
+    assert_includes @config.env.secret_keys, "SMTP_PASSWORD"
+    assert_empty @config.env.clear.keys & @config.env.secret_keys
+    template = File.read("#{@root}/.kamal/secrets.example")
+    @config.env.secret_keys.each do |key|
+      assert_match(/^#{key}=/, template)
+    end
+    assert_includes File.readlines("#{@root}/.gitignore", chomp: true), "/.kamal/secrets"
+    assert_includes File.readlines("#{@root}/.dockerignore", chomp: true), "/.kamal/"
+  end
+  def test_kamal_resolves_secrets_without_putting_them_in_clear_env
+    Dir.mktmpdir do |directory|
+      path = File.join(directory, "secrets")
+      File.write(path, "SECRET_KEY_BASE=test-key\nSMTP_USERNAME=test-user\nSMTP_PASSWORD='password with spaces # and symbols'\n")
+      config = Kamal::Configuration.new(@raw.to_h.merge(secrets_path: path), version: "test")
+      assert_equal "test-key", config.env.to_h.fetch("SECRET_KEY_BASE")
+      assert_equal "password with spaces # and symbols", config.env.to_h.fetch("SMTP_PASSWORD")
+      refute_includes config.env.clear.keys, "SMTP_PASSWORD"
+    end
+  end
+
+  def test_production_smtp_and_https_urls
+    assert_production_config({
+      "APP_FQDN" => "fizzy.example.test",
+      "SMTP_ADDRESS" => "smtp.example.test",
+      "SMTP_USERNAME" => "test-user",
+      "SMTP_PASSWORD" => "test-password"
+    }, <<~'CODE')
+      expected_url = { host: "fizzy.example.test", protocol: "https" }
+      raise "Wrong mail URL" unless ActionMailer::Base.default_url_options == expected_url
+      raise "Wrong controller URL" unless ActionController::Base.default_url_options == expected_url
+      smtp = ActionMailer::Base.smtp_settings
+      expected_smtp = ["smtp.example.test", 587, "fizzy.example.test", "test-user", "test-password", "plain", true, false]
+      raise "Wrong SMTP configuration" unless smtp.values_at(:address, :port, :domain, :user_name, :password, :authentication, :enable_starttls_auto, :ssl) == expected_smtp
+      raise "Wrong delivery method" unless ActionMailer::Base.delivery_method == :smtp
+      raise "SSL disabled" unless Rails.application.config.force_ssl && Rails.application.config.assume_ssl
+      raise "Wrong storage" unless Rails.application.config.active_storage.service == :local
+      raise "Wrong queue" unless Rails.application.config.active_job.queue_adapter == :solid_queue
+      databases = ActiveRecord::Base.configurations.configs_for(env_name: "production")
+      raise "Missing databases" unless databases.map(&:name).sort == %w[ cable cache primary queue ]
+      databases.each do |database|
+        path = File.expand_path(database.database, Rails.root)
+        raise "Database outside volume" unless database.adapter == "sqlite3" && path.start_with?(Rails.root.join("storage").to_s + "/")
+      end
+      raise "Uploads outside volume" unless ActiveStorage::Blob.service.root.to_s == Rails.root.join("storage/production/files").to_s
+    CODE
+  end
+
+  def test_production_smtp_implicit_tls
+    assert_production_config({
+      "SMTP_ADDRESS" => "smtp.example.test", "SMTP_PORT" => "465",
+      "SMTP_DOMAIN" => "mail.example.test", "SMTP_AUTHENTICATION" => "login",
+      "SMTP_SSL" => "true", "SMTP_ENABLE_STARTTLS_AUTO" => "false"
+    }, <<~'CODE')
+      smtp = ActionMailer::Base.smtp_settings
+      raise "Wrong TLS configuration" unless smtp.values_at(:port, :ssl, :enable_starttls_auto, :authentication, :domain) == [465, true, false, "login", "mail.example.test"]
+    CODE
+  end
+
+  def test_production_unauthenticated_relay
+    assert_production_config({
+      "SMTP_ADDRESS" => "relay.example.test", "SMTP_PORT" => "25", "SMTP_AUTHENTICATION" => ""
+    }, <<~'CODE')
+      smtp = ActionMailer::Base.smtp_settings
+      raise "Relay requires authentication" unless smtp.values_at(:authentication, :user_name, :password) == [nil, nil, nil]
+      raise "Wrong relay port" unless smtp[:port] == 25
+    CODE
+  end
+
+  def test_production_can_boot_without_deployment_variables
+    assert_production_config({}, 'raise "Unexpected mail hostname" if ActionMailer::Base.default_url_options&.key?(:host)')
+  end
+
+  private
+    def assert_production_config(env, code)
+      # Never use the developer's real SMTP credentials or SaaS configuration.
+      clean_env = %w[ APP_FQDN SMTP_ADDRESS SMTP_PORT SMTP_DOMAIN SMTP_USERNAME SMTP_PASSWORD SMTP_AUTHENTICATION SMTP_SSL SMTP_ENABLE_STARTTLS_AUTO DISABLE_SSL ASSUME_SSL FORCE_SSL ACTIVE_STORAGE_SERVICE ].to_h { |key| [ key, nil ] }
+      clean_env.merge!("SAAS" => "false", "RAILS_ENV" => "production", "DATABASE_ADAPTER" => "sqlite", "SECRET_KEY_BASE" => "deployment-test-only")
+      output, status = Open3.capture2e(clean_env.merge(env), "bundle", "exec", "rails", "runner", code, chdir: @root)
+      assert status.success?, output
+    end
+end
